R76/2006 standard.\" I can include description.\n\nrecommendation: id \"R76\", edition 2006, scheme omitted, accuracy_classes [\"III\"].\n\nShould I include `characteristics.type_level.accuracy_class` AND recommendation.accuracy_classes? Both fine.\n\nDate formats: date_issued \"2017-11-27\". Test report date \"2016-09-12\".\n\nRevision history: not present. Footnotes: none defined.\n\nThe \"Thank you\" chatbot commentary — ignore. The \"Summary:\" at the end — ignore (though it confirms three instrument families VG, VD, VO).\n\nLet me now write the JSON.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R76/2006-DK3-17.09\",\n    \"page_total\": 3,\n    \"member_state\": \"Denmark\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2017-11-27\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"DK3\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"DELTA, OIML Issuing Authority DK3\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Venlighedsvej 4\", \"2970 Hørsholm\", \"Denmark\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"J. Hovgård Jensen\",\n    \"person_title\": \"Certification Manager\",\n    \"phone\": \"+45 7219 4000\",\n    \"email\": \"weighing@delta.dk\",\n    \"website\": \"www.madebydelta.com\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"DK3\"\n  },\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Non-automatic weighing instrument\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"VGM\",\"VGW\",\"NGP\",\"VGC\",\"VDM\",\"VDW\",\"VDP\",\"VDC\",\"VOM\",\"VOWK\",\"VOP\",\"VOC\"],\n    \"description\": \"Non-automatic weighing instrument (indicator) under OIML R 76; software identification displayed during power-up sequence\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": null,\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"VGM\", \"label\": \"VGM\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"WEIGHING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE020\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VGW\", \"label\": \"VGW\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"CHECKWEIGHING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE004\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"NGP\", \"label\": \"NGP\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"PRICE COMPUTING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE005\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VGC\", \"label\": \"VGC\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"PARTS COUNTING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE006\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VDM\", \"label\": \"VDM\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"WEIGHING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE011\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VDW\", \"label\": \"VDW\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"CHECKWEIGHING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE012\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VDP\", \"label\": \"VDP\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"PRICE COMPUTING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE013\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VDC\", \"label\": \"VDC\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"PARTS COUNTING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE014\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VOM\", \"label\": \"VOM\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"WEIGHING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE007\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VOWK\", \"label\": \"VOWK\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"CHECKWEIGHING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE008\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VOP\", \"label\": \"VOP\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"PRICE COMPUTING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE009\"}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"VOC\", \"label\": \"VOC\", \"attributes\": {\"application\": \"PARTS COUNTING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE010\"}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Approved software identification by model\",\n      \"columns\": [\"model_name\", \"application\", \"software_identification\"],\n      \"rows\": [\n        {\"model_name\": \"VGM\", \"application\": \"WEIGHING\", \"software_identification\": \"CE020\"},\n        ... all 12\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"III\"},\n      \"weighing_range\": {\"value\": \"single-interval or dual-range\"},\n      \"maximum_capacity\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 1.5, \"max\": 30}, \"unit_symbol\": \"kg\"},\n      \"minimum_capacity\": {\"value\": 20, \"unit_symbol\": \"e\"},\n      \"verification_scale_interval\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.5, \"max\": null}, \"unit_symbol\": \"g\"},\n      \"subtractive_tare\": {\"value\": \"-Max\"},\n      \"interface\": {\"value\": \"Protective according to paragraph 5.3.6\"},\n      \"supply_voltage\": {\"value\": 9, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n      \"power_supply_type\": {\"value\": \"DC from external adapter; optional 6 V internal battery\"},\n      \"adapter_input_voltage\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 100, \"max\": 240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n      \"adapter_input_frequency\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 50, \"max\": 60}, \"unit_symbol\": \"Hz\"},\n      \"battery_voltage\": {\"value\": 6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n      \"common_software_version\": {\"value\": \"1.02xx (xx = 00 to 99)\"}\n    },\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\n        \"attribute\": \"max_number_of_intervals\",\n        \"axis\": \"weighing range configuration\",\n        \"values\": [\n          {\"condition\": \"single-interval\", \"value\": 6000},\n          {\"condition\": \"dual-range (per range)\", \"value\": 3000}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R76\",\n    \"edition\": 2006,\n    \"accuracy_classes\": [\"III\"]\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"DANAK-1916850\",\n      \"date\": \"2016-09-12\",\n      \"pages\": 60,\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWait — the value objects in config_level: schema says values follow same structured form {condition, value, unit_symbol}. Value 6000 number. OK.\n\nThe `subtractive_tare` \"-Max\": maybe better written as \"≤ -Max\"? Original \"≤ −Max\". I'll use value \"-Max\" — since \"subtractive tare T ≤ −Max\". Hmm, ambiguous. Keep \"-Max\" string.\n\nAlso `maximum_capacity` attribute label — original \"Maximum capacity Maxᵢ\". Canonical: `maximum_capacity`. Fine. `minimum_capacity_min_i` → `minimum_capacity`. `verification_scale_interval_ei` → `verification_scale_interval`. `number_of_intervals_max_i_over_ei` → `max_number_of_intervals`. OK.\n\nShould power_supply_type be a separate \"DC\"? I combined into a string. Rules say split power supply into voltage/frequency/type. I have supply_voltage (9 V DC). Let me do:\n- supply_voltage: 9 V\n- power_supply_type: \"DC (external adapter); optional internal battery\"\nThat's fine, or split battery separately. I'll include both battery_voltage and power_supply_type string \"DC\". Keep it consistent:\n\n- power_supply_type: {\"value\": \"DC\"}\n- supply_voltage: 9, V\n- battery_voltage: 6, V (optional — add a string? value 6, unit V). The \"optional\" nuance lost; add attribute `battery`: \"optional 6 V internal battery\"? To keep clean, I'll include battery_voltage with value 6 and mention optional in power_supply_type: \"DC (external adapter) or optional internal battery\". Hmm.\n\nSimplest: \n- supply_voltage: {\"value\": 9, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n- power_supply_type: {\"value\": \"DC external adapter; optional 6 V internal battery\"}\n- adapter_input_voltage: {\"value\": {\"min\":100,\"max\":240}, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n- adapter_input_frequency: {\"value\": {\"min\":50,\"max\":60}, \"unit_symbol\": \"Hz\"}\n- battery_voltage: {\"value\": 6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n\nSlight redundancy with battery mentioned twice — drop battery from power_supply_type: power_supply_type: {\"value\": \"DC (external adapter)\"}. Good.\n\nThe footnote stuff — none.\n\nAlso \"Software identification Legal SW / application SW / other | See page 3\" — that's a pointer, covered by description/table. Skip as characteristic.\n\nAlso \"certificate applies to non-automatic weighing instrument (indicator)\" — the summary at the end mentions it; it's in the page-2 transcription section. Fine.\n\nEdition: R76/2006 → edition 2006. int per schema (edition (int)). Good.\n\nTest report issuer \"DELTA, DK\" — could add to test report? Schema has only id, date, pages, role. Keep those.\n\nFinal JSON. Ensure no markdown fences, parseable.",
